    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d225">

                <pb facs="0418" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.113 Senate Investigation/213</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Special Committee of the Senate
                        Investigating the Munitions Industry</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Nye</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to Mr.
                            Joseph C. Green of the Division of
                        Western European Affairs</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-02-20">February 20,
                        1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Green</hi>: It is hoped by the Committee
                    that in the course of your work at the State Department, it will be possible for
                    you to prepare a memorandum covering the problems which will be raised by the
                    adoption of any international convention for the control of arms. I refer to the
                    difficulties attendant upon the securing of constitutional legislation of a
                    purely national character, either in advance of such convention or to supplement
                    such a convention.</p>
                <p>The Committee would appreciate any assistance you could, in the normal course of
                    your duties, render to it along these lines, and I would be glad, if you so
                    desire, to address a letter to this effect to the Secretary of State.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerald P. Nye</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
